 "notes": "Piece N1 (edge-pieces assignment): Geneva Avenue at the county line. 23 block polygons, 1 open polygon. Box: the given 1700,3640,640,295 with the bottom trimmed 5 px (h 290, last row y 3929) so the whole box lies above the county line: that line's top is at y 3934 on the left but rises to y 3930 at x 2330, so with h 295 the last row at x > 2100 lay beyond it. The top 100 rows (y < 3740) are held out and outlined all the same.\nTHE TRIANGLE (polygon, the reason for this piece): sides (1) Geneva Ave's south line, from its corner at (1829,3867) to the box bottom at (2007,3929); (2) the thin line on its west, (1829,3867) to (1806,3929), the east line of the street that runs south from Geneva between 6428 and the triangle; (3) the bottom line at y 3934-3936, which lies just below the box, so the triangle is cut by the box's bottom edge. That bottom line is ONE printed line, solid at x 1827-1949 and 1995-2114 and broken into dashes at x 1950-1994 (the county line's dashes); no second line is printed below it, only blank paper (y 3937-4000) down to the sheet's heavy rule. No number is printed in the triangle.\nStreet west of the triangle (x 1798-1818 at y 3900): 6428's east line, a 3 px strip, a heavy zoning border (x 1804-1811), a 4 px strip, the triangle's west line: all street (the border runs in the roadway).\nThe road from the north-west into Geneva (x 1700-1830, y 3725-3860, between the 6328 strip and Wallbridge): NE strip, heavy zoning border, SW strip (x 1746-1759 at y 3800) closed by a thin line. Wallbridge (named, 1705-1820, 3808-3858) opens into the SW strip, so that strip is roadway: all street.\nOPEN polygon, the wedge (1700-1775, 3753-3832): land south-west of that road's thin SW line and north of Wallbridge, with no outline of its own in the box and no number; it runs on west outside the box into the land printed RH-2 around block 6423 (about 1560-1700, 3820-3935). Most likely land, so open; it may be part of a block whose outline lies outside the box.\n6328 is typed as TWO polygons: the strip (1700-1767, 3696-3757) and the piece east of it (1784-1872, 3706-3747) both carry 6328, but the big block's notch, edged by a heavy zoning border (1745-1784, 3712-3744), reaches down to the street line, leaving only ink (1767-1784, 3744-3751) between them.\nThe big block top left (1700-1880, 3640-3745, no number in the box) is separated from 6328 and from 6315's tip (1840-1905, 3640-3695) by heavy borders over block lines (different numbers either side): separate polygons, typed 1 px apart along the middle of the heavy line. Likewise 6313 against 6331 and 6332, and 6312 against 6374 (heavy line x 2245-2268, y 3760-3830).\nHeavy zoning borders inside one block do not split it: 6311 includes the heavy-bordered lot (2283-2321, 3665-3725) and the sliver cut off by the I of RM-I (2167-2176, 3640-3664); 6312 includes the corner lot inside the heavy L (2269-2299, 3740-3770); 6428 includes its NC-S part below the heavy line (1700-1800, 3878-3929); 6323 and 6322 include the NC-1 strip south of the heavy line (2005-2145, 3876-3929).\nNC-1 (2005-2090, 3878-3929): taken as land of 6323 (a zoning district, its left side continuing 6323's west line); Geneva runs below its bottom heavy line, and the sliver of Geneva there (2005-2080, 3912-3929) is street. DOUBTFUL: Santos St (x 2080-2100 at y 3890) seems to end at the NC-1 heavy line (2080-2095, 3893-3905): below it no west line is printed, only the slanted 1 of NC-1 (2070-2081, 3905-3925), and 6322's west line curving into its south face (2081,3908)-(2113,3935). Typed so (6323's NC-1 part reaches east to 6322's line). If Santos is meant to reach Geneva, the strip (2075-2088, 3905-3929) should be street.\nNarrow streets with a heavy border down the middle, all street: between 6321 and 6320 (x 2202-2246), between 6320 and 6319 (x 2280-2300; 6320's own line is the inner thin one, x 2291 at y 3865 to 2270 at y 3929), and the band north of 6323-6321 along the heavy diagonal (Sunrise Way's west end, 2062-2290, 3770-3830).\nTop right (held-out rows): the narrow strip (2327-2339, 3640-3676) between 6311's east line and a second line is left as street (it continues the street along 6311's top, above the box); the street east of 6311 and 6312 (2290-2339, 3672-3793) is street.\nLetters, block numbers and zoning letters were ignored; streets keep their lettering and the heavy borders in them.\nHow the corners were placed: each printed area's paper was grown up to 4 px into its own line (where two blocks share a line, split at its middle and typed 1 px apart), closed over letters and over the heavy borders inside one block, and simplified to within 1 px, with a scratch script outside the repository; every block was then checked against 4x close-ups.",
